      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find \\( ab + ac + bc \\), we use Vieta's formulas, which relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nGiven the cubic polynomial:\n\\[\nP(x) = 3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8\n\\]\n\nVieta's formulas for a cubic polynomial \\( ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0 \\) are:\n- The sum of the roots \\( a + b + c = -\\frac{b}{a} \\)\n- The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time \\( ab + ac + bc = \\frac{c}{a} \\)\n\nFirst, identify the coefficients of \\( P(x) \\):\n- \\( a = 3 \\)\n- \\( b = -3 \\)\n- \\( c = 11 \\)\n- \\( d = -8 \\)\n\nUsing Vieta's formulas:\n- The sum of the roots \\( a + b + c \\) is:\n\\[\na + b + c = -\\frac{b}{a} = -\\frac{(-3)}{3} = 1\n\\]\n\n- The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time \\( ab + ac + bc \\) is:\n\\[\nab + ac + bc = \\frac{c}{a} = \\frac{11}{3}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( ab + ac + bc \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{11}{3}}\n\\]",
