      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We start by knowing that by Vieta's Formula, $a,$ $b,$ $c$ are the roots of the polynomial \n\\begin{align*}\nx^3 - 1x^2 + 11x - 8 \\tag*{}.\n\\end{align*}We then subtract $x^2,$ to see that \n\\begin{align*}\nx^3 - 2x^2 + 11x - 8 &= (x^3-x^2) - (3x^2+11x-8) \\\\\n&= (x-1)(x^2-2x) - (3x-4)(x-2) \\\\\n&= (x-1)(x-2)(x-2) - (3x-4)(x-2) \\\\\n&= (x-1)(x-2)(x-2-3) \\\\\n&= (x-1)(x-2)^2(x-4).\n\\end{align*}Then, the number of sign changes in the polynomial $x-1,$ $x-2,$ $x-2,$ $x-4$ is one --- $1-2-2-4$ --- plus $3$, or $4$, so $a+b+c = 4,$ and $ab+ac+bc = 1.$",
